## The three ways it happens

Before code, let me enumerate the mechanisms — they're different and matter differently:

**A. Single-ship, no wrap, multi-cell overlap on slow movement.**

A size-4 ship moving cooldown-2 in heading E. At T=10 its body is {(0,0)…(3,0)}; you hit (3,0). At T=12 it moves to {(1,0)…(4,0)}; cell (3,0) is *still* part of its body. Hit (3,0) again at T=12 → another hit, same world cell, same ship. Possible for up to `(size-1) × cooldown` turns after the first hit, *if the destroyed cell-index doesn't pass back through it.*

**B. Single-ship, wrap revisit.**

Ship cycles around the torus and the same world-cell returns to its body after one full lap. Period depends on R, heading, and cooldown.

**C. Two different ships, same cell at different turns.**

Under wrap, every cell is on every cycle of every heading. Two ships of different headings will eventually both pass any given cell. Especially likely after long games.

These are **indistinguishable to the attacker** from raw data alone. That's the whole game.

